~ start
There is nothing to tie around her. Ollie grabs Noni's wrist with both hands.
Ollie: Climb! I've got you!
Noni: It hurts! Ollie, you're pulling too hard!
A sharp cry. Her arm twists wrong as she is dragged over the ledge.
Noni: My arm! My arm!
Ollie: I'm sorry! I'm sorry, just a little more!
Noni: ...I'm up. It hurts so much.
Ollie: If I'd brought the rope, this wouldn't have happened.
Ollie: It's my fault.



=> END